        "problem": "Identify the surface $6{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12x+8y-10=0.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12x+8y-10 & =0 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-2x)-4({y}^{2}-2y)-6{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ 6[(x-1)^{2}-1]-4[(y-1)^{2}-1]-6{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)^{2}-6-4(y-1)^{2}+4-6{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(x-1)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2}-6{z}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(1,1,0).$",
